## When

Triggered by: {{triggers}} — see [01]({{ref_01}}). Deep review for {{deep_areas}}.

## Order

1. Fix the revision; stay read-only ([01]({{ref_01}})).
2. Write the threat model for the change ([02]({{ref_02}})).
3. Fill the authorization matrix; check data scopes ([03]({{ref_03}})).
4. Run the checks for the branch ([04]({{ref_04}})).
5. Findings as exploit scenarios → sign-off ([05]({{ref_05}})).
6. Report through the approved channel ([06]({{ref_06}})).

## Sign-off

| Findings | Verdict |
|---|---|
| CONFIRMED CRITICAL / HIGH | `{{changes_word}}` |
| PLAUSIBLE CRITICAL / HIGH | `{{blocked_word}}` until the named evidence arrives |
| MEDIUM / LOW only | `{{approved_word}}` with findings listed (fixed when cheap) |
| None | `{{approved_word}}` — "no security finding" |

## Never

- Exploit shared or production environments, or use real credentials/personal data in tests or reports.
- Edit code or tests during the review.
- Report a finding without an exploit scenario.

